{"id":"ea87f2f412f451b0","group":"67","path":"67/67-thm-negated-consistency-conservative.md","title":"Negated Consistency Is Pi-One Conservative","display":"thm-negated-consistency-conservative — Negated Consistency Is Pi-One Conservative","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-thm-negated-consistency-conservative","aliases":["67-thm-negated-consistency-conservative"],"display":"thm-negated-consistency-conservative — Negated Consistency Is Pi-One Conservative","depends_on":["[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","[[67-df-consistency-statement]]","[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","[[67-thm-formalized-second-incompleteness]]","[[67-df-PA]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":5,"source_label":"Theorem 5.1","source_printed_pages":[62],"source_pdf_pages":[73],"verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source-statement-checked; proof scope and outstanding obligations in Remark","eligible_as_verified_dependency":false},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-thm-negated-consistency-conservative"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-thm-negated-consistency-conservative</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-negated-consistency-conservative — Negated Consistency Is Pi-One Conservative"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d404f437f90ff5f6\" href=\"?note=d404f437f90ff5f6\" title=\"67-df-consistency-statement\">67-df-consistency-statement</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f79515ad9f47279a\" href=\"?note=f79515ad9f47279a\" title=\"67-thm-formalized-second-incompleteness\">67-thm-formalized-second-incompleteness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"cd051851df5d2aa2\" href=\"?note=cd051851df5d2aa2\" title=\"67-df-PA\">67-df-PA</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"5"},{"key":"source_label","html":"Theorem 5.1"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-statement-checked; proof scope and outstanding obligations in Remark"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\">\\(T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\\)</span> 采用固定 PR 呈示和标准证明算术化；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}_T\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d404f437f90ff5f6\" href=\"?note=d404f437f90ff5f6\" title=\"67-df-consistency-statement\">67-df-consistency-statement</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi_1\">\\(\\Pi_1\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_1}\">\\(\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_1}\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a>。不增加外部一致性或 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1\">\\(\\Sigma_1\\)</span> 可靠性假设。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_1}(\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T,T).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_1}(\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T,T).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书印刷62页/PDF73页定理1。若 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\\in\\Pi_1\">\\(\\pi\\in\\Pi_1\\)</span> 且 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\\vdash\\pi\">\\(T+\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\\vdash\\pi\\)</span>，则 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Con}_T\">\\(T\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Con}_T\\)</span>。形式化可证明性及可证 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1\">\\(\\Sigma_1\\)</span> 完备性给出 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PA}\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Prov}_T(\\ulcorner\\mathrm{Con}_T\\urcorner)\">\\(\\mathrm{PA}\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Prov}_T(\\ulcorner\\mathrm{Con}_T\\urcorner)\\)</span>；形式化第二不完全性使之蕴涵 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\">\\(\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\\)</span>。另一方面 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Con}_T\">\\(T\\vdash\\neg\\pi\\to\\mathrm{Con}_T\\)</span>，故 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\pi\">\\(T\\vdash\\pi\\)</span>。</p>\n<p>这是后果保守性，不是声称 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\">\\(\\neg\\mathrm{Con}_T\\)</span> 为真。来源的短推导已读并记录；自然证明算术化和形式化可证完备性的完整基础链未独立重建。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-partially-conservative","status":"resolved","id":"5d04e3c8a5885c18","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-consistency-statement","status":"resolved","id":"d404f437f90ff5f6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-consistency-statement]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-arithmetical-classes","status":"resolved","id":"851cd80e64893935","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-thm-formalized-second-incompleteness","status":"resolved","id":"f79515ad9f47279a","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-thm-formalized-second-incompleteness]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-PA","status":"resolved","id":"cd051851df5d2aa2","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-PA]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-consistency-statement","status":"resolved","id":"d404f437f90ff5f6","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}$ 采用固定 PR 呈示和标准证明算术化；$\\mathrm{Con}_T$ 取 [[67-df-consistency-statement]]。","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-arithmetical-classes","status":"resolved","id":"851cd80e64893935","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Pi_1$ 取 [[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]；$\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_1}$ 取 [[67-df-partially-conservative]]。不增加外部一致性或 $\\Sigma_1$ 可靠性假设。","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-partially-conservative","status":